     "date": "2026-09-04T12:34:19Z"
    },
    "message": "ci(desktop): make SHA256SUMS-desktop-shell.txt one format on all four runners\n\nThe first successful four-platform release (run 33871599947) attached a\nchecksum file with three lines in one format and one in another:\n\n    5788...f0f8  MyClaudeCode-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\n    b4d8...a478 *MyClaudeCode-windows-x86_64.zip\n\nGit for Windows' sha256sum defaults to binary mode and writes `<digest>\n*<name>`; GNU coreutils on Linux writes `<digest>  <name>`. Both are valid\ninput to `sha256sum -c`, which is why the verification step passed, and both\nwere documented as one format, which was wrong. A file whose shape depends on\nwhich runner produced which line is not a contract S4 can parse.\n\nEach leg now builds its line from the digest with printf instead of printing\nwhatever its sha256sum felt like emitting, and the aggregating job asserts\nevery line is 64 hex characters, two spaces and a filename before uploading --\nso a stray mode marker fails the release rather than surfacing in Python\nmonths later.\n\nThe README's example is now four real lines from that release rather than an\nelided sketch, and says why the line is rebuilt.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JsSZ8AQXV1XKgKkgYBU5UT",
    "tree": {
